<si-x data-si-tag="p" class="lab-why bz" data-l10n="" data-en="&lt;b&gt;Why it’s built this way: &lt;/b&gt;The model’s parameters don’t change in use, so it doesn’t know your company’s rules. Store the documents ahead of time, find the most relevant chunks at question time and put them into the context — then the model can “answer from the documents” and even cite sources." data-bz="1"><ul class="pts"><li><b>Why it’s built this way: </b>The model’s parameters don’t change in use, so it doesn’t know your company’s rules.</li><li>Store the documents ahead of time, find the most relevant chunks at question time and put them into the context — then the model can “answer from the documents” and even cite sources.</li></ul></si-x>
